        // via a third party, deployer cannot cancel (loses PROPOSER).
        // In reference, renounce from third party reverts, deployer keeps PROPOSER and can cancel.

        // Reset: Use fresh scenario
        // Re-deploy? Cannot in test. Let's compute from current state.

        // Actually simpler: Test the cancel function directly.
        // After renouncing PROPOSER_ROLE from address(this) using buggy renounce (allowed),
        // address(this) tries to cancel -> reference: renounce reverts so address(this) still has role -> can cancel
        // buggy: renounce succeeds, address(this) loses role -> cancel reverts

